<b>10 Years of GPU Viewer</b>
GPU Viewer began as a Linux graphics information front end in 2017. Over the decade, the project has grown from an easier way to browse command-line graphics output into a modern GTK4/libadwaita application with dedicated graphics, monitoring, API, distribution, and system views.
Thank you to everyone who reported bugs, contributed code, packaged GPU Viewer for Linux distributions, shared feedback, and supported the project.

GPU Viewer is a graphical front end for the command-line outputs of glxinfo, vulkaninfo, clinfo, es2_info, and vdpauinfo. It helps users browse and compare OpenGL, Vulkan, OpenCL, EGL, Vulkan Video, VDPAU, device, driver, distribution, and system information.

GPU Viewer does not implement OpenGL, Vulkan, or OpenCL application functionality. The application primarily displays structured information returned by the system utilities listed below.

