This program uses:
    - Python 3 or higher
    - GTK4 and libadwaita for the graphical user interface
    - Cairo and PyGObject for graphics, widgets, and Python bindings
    - Meson for building and installing the application
    - glxinfo and related Mesa tools for OpenGL, OpenGL ES, GLX, and EGL information
    - vulkaninfo for Vulkan devices, capabilities, extensions, formats, memory, queues, and instance information
    - Vulkan Video information for supported codecs and video capabilities
    - clinfo for OpenCL platforms, devices, memory, queues, extensions, and capabilities
    - vdpauinfo for VDPAU information when supported
    - lscpu for CPU information
    - lsb_release for distribution information
    - XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP for desktop environment information
    - XDG_SESSION_TYPE for the graphical session and windowing system
    - cat /proc/meminfo and awk for memory information
    - uname for kernel information

<b>GPU Viewer features:</b>
    - Dashboard and GPU-Z-style graphics information views
    - Multi-GPU detection, selection, and per-GPU information
    - Real-time hardware and sensor monitoring
    - GPU, CPU, memory, distribution, desktop, and kernel details
    - API support indicators for Vulkan, OpenGL, EGL, OpenCL, Vulkan Video, VDPAU, Ray Tracing, and Mesh Shaders
    - Vulkan device properties, features, limits, extensions, formats, memory, queues, and instance information
    - OpenCL platform, device, memory, vector, queue, execution, extension, SPIR-V, and IL information
    - OpenGL, OpenGL ES, GLX frame-buffer configuration, limits, extensions, and EGL information
    - Vulkan Video, VDPAU, codec, encoder, decoder, surface, and feature information
    - Collapsible navigation sidebars in Vulkan, Vulkan Video, OpenGL, OpenCL, and VDPAU views
    - Vendor, GPU, distribution, desktop environment, and graphics technology logos
    - Automatic light and dark theme support
    - Expandable trees, searchable columns, and responsive GPU-Z cards

